{"id": "EUVD-2026-80400", "enisaUuid": "fe8a1e18-3ea5-3607-ba48-b13c2596d6a3", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/nouveau/uvmm: clear the dirty flag when unwinding an OP_UNMAP_SPARSE\n\nA successful OP_UNMAP_SPARSE marks its region dirty with\nnouveau_uvma_region_dirty() and defers the teardown to\nnouveau_uvmm_bind_job_cleanup(); it does not remove the region from\nuvmm->region_mt.\n\nIf a later op in the job fails, the unwind path never clears reg->dirty\n(set in one place, cleared nowhere) and sets op->reg = NULL, so cleanup\nskips the teardown. The region is left in the tree with dirty set and its\ncompletion never signalled. Later binds over that range then fail\npermanently -- -ENOENT or -EINVAL from the dirty checks, or an unkillable\nwait_for_completion() in bind_validate_region() -- for the lifetime of\nthe uvmm.\n\nClear reg->dirty when the unwind reverts the sparse unmap, restoring the\nregion to the state it was found in.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T10:30:33", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:52:54", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a129b2b875c148aba233ace8447a0c36ca3bae07", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/196ce9e5e93202da097062be24e404984dbc5ac2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1101cbfe7f342e5eaaf7444965d4f1215abdac4c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c60033c172420179b7bbb3d1f843f8dc90164dc5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/38a62306c4266bcb3cd89e33c7111ee33096ebb3"], "aliases": ["GHSA-g7qr-ggg3-47g8", "CVE-2026-89800"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "02a795be-6711-3312-a164-3696b1974028", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b88baab828713ce0b49b185444b2ee83bed373a8 <c60033c172420179b7bbb3d1f843f8dc90164dc5"}, {"id": "09a26f6f-102c-3499-964e-3d75c81a67da", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b88baab828713ce0b49b185444b2ee83bed373a8 <a129b2b875c148aba233ace8447a0c36ca3bae07"}, {"id": "12f4cf8a-c010-30f7-928c-d2d4ef8ab414", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6"}, {"id": "145aea61-9183-3a57-9cb8-4e10be41c6bd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.51"}, {"id": "1688e776-40a7-3a1a-b403-04d00834fa2b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "41baa6fe-38a3-3370-8ca7-6245bfa8214e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b88baab828713ce0b49b185444b2ee83bed373a8 <38a62306c4266bcb3cd89e33c7111ee33096ebb3"}, {"id": "4d1f2114-3032-36ca-a122-8e7dd14ef37d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b88baab828713ce0b49b185444b2ee83bed373a8 <196ce9e5e93202da097062be24e404984dbc5ac2"}, {"id": "81bf7376-2e24-35cf-98b6-97d398c9f5b3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "a211529a-112a-3f08-867a-31774c9ecea4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "a2e38d51-b551-331c-b688-9caa8a84cc3e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "b6c196f0-2783-363f-89e5-6f517cbfae3c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.5"}, {"id": "eefe8c46-1cae-34dc-9616-994d295ab656", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b88baab828713ce0b49b185444b2ee83bed373a8 <1101cbfe7f342e5eaaf7444965d4f1215abdac4c"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "4289cd3f-6552-39d4-8384-f8c9e9626e6e", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}